✅ ✅ 21. What is loop in Ansible and how it is used ?
👉 Loop is used to repeat a task multiple times with different values
✅ Used when:

creating multiple users
installing multiple packages
executing same task for multiple items

✅ Example:
- name: Install packages
  ansible.builtin.package:
    name: "{{ item }}"
    state: present
  loop:
    - httpd
    - git
    - vim

👉 item represents each value

✅ ✅ 22. What is conditional task in Ansible ?
👉 Conditional tasks are used to run tasks only when a condition is true
✅ Uses:
when

✅ Example:
- name: Install httpd only on RedHat
  ansible.builtin.package:
    name: httpd
    state: present
  when: ansible_os_family == "RedHat"


✅ ✅ 23. What is handler and use of notify keyword ?
👉 Handler is a special task that runs only when notified
👉 notify is used to trigger handler

✅ Example:
tasks:
  - name: Update config file
    ansible.builtin.copy:
      src: file.conf
      dest: /etc/file.conf
    notify: restart service

handlers:
  - name: restart service
    ansible.builtin.service:
      name: httpd
      state: restarted

👉 Handler runs only if task changes something ✅

